\noindent\textbf{Shimento}\hfill Hyderabad, India\\
\textit{Fullstack AI Engineer}\hfill Nov 2025 -- Jun 2026
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Agentic AI Systems:} Designed and implemented agent-based workflows using LangChain and LangGraph for complex reasoning, validation, and tool orchestration.
\item \textbf{VS Code Extension:} Developed a VS Code extension using TypeScript to provide AI-assisted code understanding, context-aware actions, and seamless backend integration.
\item \textbf{Backend AI Services:} Built scalable Python backend services using FastAPI to handle LangChain-based computation, agent execution, and structured LLM outputs.
\item \textbf{LLM Integrations:} Integrated OpenAI/AzureOpenAI models with deterministic JSON schema validation using Pydantic to ensure reliable and reproducible AI responses.
\item \textbf{System Design:} Designed end-to-end fullstack architecture connecting editor extensions, AI agents, and backend services with robust error handling and observability.
\end{itemize}
\noindent\textbf{UBS}\hfill Pune, India\\
\textit{Software Engineer}\hfill Aug 2023 -- Nov 2025
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{LLM-Powered Code Analyzer:} Developed a Python application using GPT-4 API to analyze and summarize large code repositories. Built deterministic JSON I/O contracts using Pydantic, and exposed via FastAPI service.
\item \textbf{Multi-Agent Workflows:} Experimented with LangChain-based pipelines to orchestrate tool calling and validation for developer-facing automation tasks.
\item \textbf{Context + Code Understanding:} Integrated AST parsing and static analysis into LLM workflows to improve accuracy of code recommendations.
\item \textbf{RAG Pipelines:} Prototyped retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) with embeddings for knowledge grounding in internal tools.
\item \textbf{Backend Integrations:} Designed REST APIs for financial systems using Spring Boot and FastAPI; ensured robust error handling and logging.
\item \textbf{Optimization:} Improved service performance via caching, query optimization, and asynchronous processing; reduced latency by 30\%.
\item \textbf{Deployment CI/CD:} Containerized services with Docker, deployed on Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) using Helm, and integrated automated pipelines with Azure DevOps.
\end{itemize}
\section*{Projects}
\noindent\textbf{Ariadne: On-Call Agent with Graph Memory}\hfill Oct 2026\\
\textit{Graph Hacks (FalkorDB) | Personal Project}
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Agent Design:} Built an on-call agent over a FalkorDB graph with nine graph tools; Cypher and graph algorithms rank the suspect commit while the LLM only chooses tools and explains, so the verdict is unchanged without the model.
\item \textbf{Measured Memory:} Resolved incidents are written back as reusable plans; across 20 alerts per arm the warm path took four tool calls and reached the same culprit as cold on all 20. Shipped an MCP server, Alertmanager webhook, hosted demo and 168 tests.
\end{itemize}
\noindent\textbf{AgriN: Digital Agriculture Advisory Network}\hfill 2026\\
\textit{Personal Project}
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Deterministic Engine:} FAO-56 evapotranspiration, soil and paddy water balance, nutrients and crop rotation are computed by code; the LLM only narrates, and a guard rejects any figure that is not in the engine output.
\item \textbf{Pipeline and ML:} Ingests weather, soil and Sentinel satellite data on a schedule; shipped an on-device rice disease model (10 classes, 0.981 accuracy on answered photos) with cloud fallback, spend caps and an offline-first mobile app.
\end{itemize}
\noindent\textbf{Jal Panchayat: Village Water Safety Verdicts}\hfill 2026\\
\textit{Code for a Billion | Personal Project}
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Fail-Closed Engine:} Deterministic IS 10500 verdict engine over 16 water-quality parameters that reports untested water as unknown, never safe; 19 property tests.
\item \textbf{Safe Narration:} Narration guard blocks invented figures and the boiling myth; reply rendering runs with no model. Public data shows 72,606 contaminated samples with remedial action recorded for 31\%.
\end{itemize}
\noindent\textbf{RoadLedger: Road Defect Measurement}\hfill 2026\\
\textit{OpenCV AI Competition 2026 | Personal Project}
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Measured Evidence:} OpenCV pipeline that rectifies the road plane and measures each defect's area in square metres, scores agreement across views and asks a person when they disagree; 41 invariant tests.
\item \textbf{Live Capture:} Phone-mounted capture mode and a review UI deployed on AWS CloudFront, producing prioritised, costed repair work orders.
\end{itemize}
